        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Let $u=\u27e8\\frac{3}{5},2,5\u27e9$ and $v=\u27e82,1,\\frac{7}{2}\u27e9.$ Find $u\\times v.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & 5 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((2)(\\frac{7}{2})-(5)(1))i-((\\frac{3}{5})(\\frac{7}{2})-(5)(2))j+((\\frac{3}{5})(1)-(2)(2))k \\\\  & =(7-(5))i-(\\frac{21}{10}-(10))j+(\\frac{3}{5}-(4))k \\\\  & =2i+\\frac{79}{10}j-\\frac{17}{5}k \\\\  & =\u27e82,\\frac{79}{10},-\\frac{17}{5}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
